For each $k \in \{1, \dots, n\}$, $(2n+1)\theta_k = (2k-1)\pi$, so $\sin\bigl((2n+1)\theta_k\bigr) = 0$. By De Moivre's expansion:
\begin{align*}
  \sin\bigl((2n+1)\theta\bigr) &= \sum_{r=0}^{n} (-1)^r \binom{2n+1}{2r+1} \cos^{2n-2r}\theta \sin^{2r+1}\theta = 0.
\end{align*}
Dividing by $\cos^{2n+1}\theta$ yields a degree-$n$ polynomial in $u = \tan^2\theta$:
\begin{align*}
  \binom{2n+1}{2n+1}u^n - \binom{2n+1}{2n-1}u^{n-1} + \cdots = 0,
\end{align*}
whose $n$ roots are $\tan^2\theta_1, \dots, \tan^2\theta_n$. By Vieta's formula:
\begin{align*}
  \sum_{k=1}^{n} \tan^2\theta_k = \binom{2n+1}{2} = n(2n+1) &\implies \sum_{k=1}^{n} |\vec{a}_k|^2 = n + n(2n+1) = 2n(n+1).
\end{align*}
Similarly, dividing by $\sin^{2n+1}\theta$ gives $\binom{2n+1}{1}v^n - \binom{2n+1}{3}v^{n-1} + \cdots = 0$ in $v = \cot^2\theta$:
\begin{align*}
